--- C. FINDING F1: lambda/routines-runner/index.test.mjs is executed by no runner ---
Confirmed by exhaustive search — zero references outside the file itself:

$ grep -rn "routines-runner" .github/ package.json vitest.config.ts scripts/ tests/ playwright.config.ts
(no matches; rc=1)

$ grep -rn "node --test" .github/ package.json scripts/
.github/workflows/ci.yml:41:        run: node --test lambda/cost-report
.github/workflows/ci.yml:48:        run: node --test lambda/agentcore-hub-jira
.github/workflows/ci.yml:55:        run: node --test lambda/anomaly-watcher
  -> routines-runner is not among the three `node --test` dirs, and its path is
     absent from vitest.config.ts include. It is also not matched by any glob in
     that array: the only lambda globs are "lambda/eval-packager/**/*.test.mjs"
     and per-file entries; every other lambda/**/*.test.mjs is listed explicitly.

Severity is raised by this epic's own change. The file is not merely legacy dead
weight — TEAM-4247 (commit 723d946, "feat(api): sweep cadence gate on scheduled
starts") ADDED 17 lines of new assertions to it inside this very range:

$ git diff --stat 4633c01..HEAD -- lambda/routines-runner/index.test.mjs
 lambda/routines-runner/index.test.mjs | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

The two new tests are:
  test("stamps trigger scheduled on every payload")
  test("index.mjs's own buildPayload stamps the trigger")   <- reads index.mjs and
      asserts /trigger:\s*"scheduled"/, i.e. the drift guard for the load-bearing
      label that the TEAM-4247 sweep cadence gate keys on ('skips ONLY
      trigger:"scheduled"' per the test's own comment).
So the drift guard protecting the epic's cadence gate never runs in CI. If
index.mjs later drops trigger:"scheduled", CI stays green and the cadence gate
silently stops matching.

The file itself is healthy — it passes when invoked manually, which is why the gap
is invisible:
$ node --test lambda/routines-runner
# tests 8 / # pass 8 / # fail 0   (exit 0)

Fix is one line — either add "lambda/routines-runner/index.test.mjs" to
vitest.config.ts include (NOTE: it uses node:test, so it would need converting to
vitest imports first), or add a `node --test lambda/routines-runner` step to
ci.yml alongside the existing three. The ci.yml route needs no source change.

